}
```
Hmm, I need to be careful. The key thing is which strings resolve as non-str. The resolveMap contains: true/false variants, null/~/Null/NULL/"", .nan/.NaN/.NAN, .inf/.Inf/.INF, +.inf/-.inf variants, and "<<".

So:
- "true","True","TRUE","false","False","FALSE" → bool
- "y","Y","yes","Yes","YES","n","N","no","No","NO","on","On","ON","off","Off","OFF" → NOT in the map (yaml.v3 removed them) ✓
- "", "~", "null", "Null", "NULL" → null
